WEBVTT

1
00:00:10.800 --> 00:00:17.588
Heidi stepped out of the cart and climbed up the steep path from Dorfli, carrying her basket.

2
00:00:17.589 --> 00:00:23.780
The baker had promised to send her suitcase up to Grandfather's the next day.

3
00:00:23.781 --> 00:00:32.192
She recognized every tree along the way, and the high tops of the mountains looked down on her like old friends.

4
00:00:32.193 --> 00:00:38.109
At last, Heidi caught sight of the hut where Peter and his grandmother lived.

5
00:00:38.110 --> 00:00:44.325
With her heart beating louder and louder, she ran up to the door and burst in.

6
00:00:44.326 --> 00:00:48.784
"Oh my!" cried a voice from the corner.

7
00:00:48.785 --> 00:00:52.952
"That was just how Heidi used to run in.

8
00:00:52.953 --> 00:00:55.856
Who is there?" asked Grannie.

9
00:00:55.857 --> 00:00:58.259
"It is I, Grannie!"

10
00:00:58.260 --> 00:01:02.616
cried Heidi, and she ran and flung her arms around her.

11
00:01:02.617 --> 00:01:06.647
Grannie was so surprised that she couldn't speak.

12
00:01:06.648 --> 00:01:10.306
She stroked Heidi's head quietly and said at last,

13
00:01:10.307 --> 00:01:16.000
"Yes, yes, that is Heidi's hair and her voice.

14
00:01:16.001 --> 00:01:20.321
It really is you. Thank God."

15
00:01:20.322 --> 00:01:25.731
Tears of joy fell from the blind woman's eyes.

16
00:01:25.732 --> 00:01:30.184
"Yes, Grannie, it's really me," answered Heidi.

17
00:01:30.185 --> 00:01:34.555
"I have come back and I am never going away again.

18
00:01:34.556 --> 00:01:39.838
And you won't have any more hard bread to eat. Look!"

19
00:01:39.839 --> 00:01:46.002
One by one, Heidi took out the white rolls and piled them on Grannie's lap.

20
00:01:46.003 --> 00:01:49.142
"What a present to bring me!"

21
00:01:49.143 --> 00:01:53.086
exclaimed Grannie as her hands touched the soft bread.

22
00:01:53.087 --> 00:01:57.429
"But you're the best present of all!"

23
00:01:57.430 --> 00:02:02.823
"I was afraid you might have died while I was gone," cried Heidi.

24
00:02:02.824 --> 00:02:06.675
"And you would never get to taste the rolls."

25
00:02:06.676 --> 00:02:09.974
Grannie smiled and stroked Heidi's cheeks.

26
00:02:09.975 --> 00:02:18.107
After a friendly pause, Heidi reached into her basket, pulled out her old straw hat, and put it on.

27
00:02:18.108 --> 00:02:25.235
She told Grannie she had to go home to Grandfather, but promised to visit the next day.

28
00:02:25.236 --> 00:02:30.370
On her way up the steep path, Heidi paused to look all around her.

29
00:02:30.371 --> 00:02:35.976
The beauty of the mountain with the rocks aglow in the sun was just as she remembered.

30
00:02:35.977 --> 00:02:44.411
She dropped her basket, threw her arms above her head, and hopped from foot to foot with pure joy.

31
00:02:44.412 --> 00:02:48.110
Then she picked up her basket and started to run.

32
00:02:48.111 --> 00:02:58.338
First she saw the tops of the fir trees, then the roof of Grandfather's hut, and at last, Grandfather sitting in his favorite seat.

33
00:02:58.339 --> 00:03:02.518
"Grandfather, Grandfather," she called.

34
00:03:02.519 --> 00:03:09.633
She ran up, jumped onto his lap, and clasped her arms about his neck.

35
00:03:09.634 --> 00:03:18.257
For the first time in years, Grandfather's eyes were moist with tears, and he had to brush them away with his hand.

36
00:03:18.258 --> 00:03:22.624
"So you have come back to me, Heidi," he said.

37
00:03:22.625 --> 00:03:26.758
"Why is that? Did they send you away?"

38
00:03:26.759 --> 00:03:31.810
"Oh no, Grandfather. Don't think that," said Heidi.

39
00:03:31.811 --> 00:03:37.425
"They were all so kind, Clara, her father, and Grandmamma.

40
00:03:37.426 --> 00:03:40.247
But I was very homesick.

41
00:03:40.248 --> 00:03:44.554
I used to get a lump in my throat as if I were choking.

42
00:03:44.555 --> 00:03:49.657
I never said anything because I didn't want to be ungrateful.

43
00:03:49.658 --> 00:03:55.788
And then, suddenly, one morning Clara's father said I could come home.

44
00:03:55.789 --> 00:03:59.056
I'm sure the letter explains it all."

45
00:03:59.057 --> 00:04:03.631
She hopped down and handed him the packet and letter from her basket.

46
00:04:03.632 --> 00:04:09.168
Then hand in hand, they went inside.

47
00:04:09.169 --> 00:04:14.616
"The packet is for you," said Grandfather after reading the letter.

48
00:04:14.617 --> 00:04:16.606
"Put it in the cupboard.

49
00:04:16.607 --> 00:04:21.097
It is money for you to buy a bed and any clothes you may need.

50
00:04:21.098 --> 00:04:27.464
And now, Heidi, do you think you can still drink milk with me?" he asked.

51
00:04:27.465 --> 00:04:30.667
Eagerly Heidi sat down on her stool.

52
00:04:30.668 --> 00:04:35.235
Grandfather filled her cup right to the brim and handed it to her.

53
00:04:35.236 --> 00:04:39.525
Holding it with two hands, Heidi drank.

54
00:04:39.526 --> 00:04:48.392
"Our milk tastes nicer than anything else in the world, Grandfather," she said and smiled.
